-#
  Multi-select theater picker (see theater_multi_picker.js). Chosen theaters
  are submitted as hidden <field_name>[] inputs; choosing none leaves the
  caller to decide (usually "all theaters"). Suggestions mix theaters with
  "All theaters tagged X" groups, which carry their member theaters inline
  in the search response and add every member.

  Locals:
    field_name  (required) — array param name, e.g. 'theater_ids'
    selected    — Array<Theater> rendered as pre-filled rows
    label       — label text above the input
    placeholder — input placeholder text
:ruby
  selected    = local_assigns.fetch(:selected, [])
  label       = local_assigns.fetch(:label, 'Theaters')
  placeholder = local_assigns.fetch(:placeholder, 'Type a theater name or tag...')
.theater-multi-picker{ data: { theater_multi_picker: true, field: field_name,
                               search_url: search_theaters_admin_analysis_index_path } }
  %label
    = label
    .grid-x
      .cell.auto
        %input.theater-multi-picker-input.input-group-field{ type: 'text', placeholder: placeholder,
                                                             autocomplete: 'off' }
      .cell.shrink{ style: 'padding-left: 0.5rem' }
        %a.theater-multi-picker-remove-all.button.alert.small{ href: '#', style: 'display:none' } Remove all
  %table.theater-multi-picker-table.hover{ style: 'display:none; margin-top: 0.5rem' }
    %tbody
      - selected.each do |theater|
        %tr
          %td= theater.name
          %td.text-right
            %a.theater-multi-picker-remove.alert{ href: '#' } remove
            %input{ type: 'hidden', name: "#{field_name}[]", value: theater.id }
